WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.020
A trout is more closely related to you than to a shark.

2
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.820
That sounds wrong, because trout and shark both look like fish.

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.400
So how can a tree show it?

4
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:21.500
A phylogenetic tree is a branching diagram of hypothesized ancestry.

5
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.560
The living species sit at its tips.

6
00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:28.473
Here is a rooted tree of five animals.

7
00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:34.693
The lamprey is the outgroup, a taxon assumed to lie outside the group being studied.

8
00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:38.293
Each place where a branch splits is a node.

9
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:43.833
A node stands for an inferred common ancestor of every lineage above it.

10
00:00:44.513 --> 00:00:47.613
The root is the ancestor of everything on the tree.

11
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:53.537
To compare two tips, trace each one back until their lines meet.

12
00:00:54.737 --> 00:01:02.637
Trout and human meet at node B. Trout and shark meet at node J. Node J is older,

13
00:01:02.637 --> 00:01:09.897
because J is ancestral to B. The most recent common ancestor is the latest node from

14
00:01:09.897 --> 00:01:10.897
which both descend.

15
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:16.077
So trout is more closely related to human, and equally to frog.

16
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:21.990
Now spin node T, so that human is drawn above frog.

17
00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.150
The node still has the same two descendants.

18
00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.450
A clade is an ancestor and all of its descendants, and every clade has the same

19
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.510
members. So the relationships have not changed.

20
00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.730
Spin node B as well, and shark no longer sits beside trout.

21
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.630
Tips that sit side by side on the page are not, for that reason, closest relatives.

22
00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.730
The sister group of trout is the frog and human clade.

23
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.810
Do not count nodes either.

24
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.410
The number of nodes between two tips depends on which other species were sampled.

25
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.270
Add five more fish, and the count between trout and human rises.

26
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.070
Their most recent common ancestor has not moved.

27
00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:11.330
Nor is any living tip more evolved than another.

28
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:18.430
The human and trout lineages have each been evolving since node B. Lampreys are not

29
00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.430
primitive animals.

30
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:23.593
A tree is a hypothesis about ancestry.

31
00:02:24.533 --> 00:02:26.853
Nobody watched these lineages split.

32
00:02:27.693 --> 00:02:34.073
The tree is estimated from characters, usually DNA or protein sequences, and it can

33
00:02:34.073 --> 00:02:35.733
be tested and overturned.

34
00:02:36.733 --> 00:02:41.193
So keep one rule. Find the most recent common ancestor.

35
00:02:42.013 --> 00:02:45.673
Do not judge relatedness by how the tips sit on the page.
